Experiment 2: Network Using Switch
1. Place 4–6 PCs and one switch in the workspace.
2. Connect all PCs to the switch using copper straight-through cables.
3. Assign IP addresses in the same subnet, such as 192.168.2.1 to 192.168.2.4.
4. Set the subnet mask to 255.255.255.0.
5. Send a Simple PDU from one PC to another.
6. Observe the packet flow in Simulation mode.
7. Check how the switch learns MAC addresses and forwards frames to the appropriate port after learning the destination.
8. Record the observations.
