Experiment 3: Network Using Both Hub and Switch
1. Place one switch, one hub, and 4–6 PCs.
2. Connect two PCs directly to the switch.
3. Connect the hub to the switch using a copper straight-through cable.
4. Connect the remaining PCs to the hub.
5. Assign all PCs IP addresses in the same subnet, such as 192.168.3.1 to 192.168.3.4.
6. Send packets between PCs connected to the switch and PCs connected to the hub.
7. Enter Simulation mode and observe frame forwarding.
8. Compare the traffic generated by the hub and switch.
