Observation: Difference Between Hub and Switch
Feature	Hub	Switch
OSI layer	Physical layer (Layer 1)	Data Link layer (Layer 2)
Forwarding	Sends incoming signals to all other ports	Forwards frames based on MAC address
Collision domain	One shared collision domain	Each port is a separate collision domain
Bandwidth	Shared among connected devices	Dedicated port bandwidth
Performance	Lower efficiency	Higher efficiency
Security	Traffic is visible on all connected ports	Unicast traffic is normally sent only to the destination port after MAC learning

Expected Simulation Output
- Hub network: When a frame arrives, the hub repeats it to all other connected ports.
- Switch network: The switch learns source MAC addresses. After learning the destination MAC address, it forwards a unicast frame only to the relevant port. Unknown unicast and broadcast frames may be flooded.
- Combined network: The switch forwards traffic toward the hub, and the hub repeats it to its other connected ports.
